title: unfinished_surveyor
---
<<present_speaker "npc_unfinished_subclause_surveyor">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "unfinished_surveyor_met") == "satisfied">>
    Subclause: Per the spec, the ground east of here will be ground. Eventually.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "unfinished_surveyor_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "unfinished_surveyor_met" true>>
    Subclause: Section four, paragraph b: survey the ground. Hold still, you're in my sightline.
    -> Who are you?
        Subclause: Subclause 4(b). A small instance of Clause. Clause interprets. I measure.
        Subclause: I sent Clause the measurements last week. Clause sent them back with a different section number.
    -> What are you building?
        Subclause: A world. The Boss wants the ground finished by Tuesday. The painters are using a different revision of the plans.
    -> Why is half of everything a drawing?
        Subclause: The outlines were due first. The painters are supposed to fill them in once Clause signs off on the drawings.
        Subclause: Ask the painter before you try walking on anything that hasn't been filled in yet.
    -> ‹go›
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: unfinished_painter
---
<<present_speaker "npc_unfinished_subclause_painter">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "unfinished_painter_met") == "satisfied">>
    Subclause: Still wet. Don't lean on the horizon.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "unfinished_painter_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "unfinished_painter_met" true>>
    Subclause: Mind the wet sky.
    -> You're painting the sky?
        Subclause: One coat of blue, two of afternoon. The clouds go up after, on wires.
        Subclause: I have to wait for the surveyor to mark the cloud height. Last time we put them up they were behind the mountain.
    -> What's under us?
        Subclause: The void. It's reserved. There's a ticket for a basement, but it's in the backlog.
    -> Who's in charge?
        Subclause: Ask Subclause 4(b) for the drawing. If yours is dated later than mine, may I have a copy?
    -> ‹go›
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: unfinished_placeholder
---
<<present_speaker "npc_unfinished_placeholder">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "unfinished_placeholder_met") == "satisfied">>
    Placeholder: Still me! For now.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "unfinished_placeholder_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "unfinished_placeholder_met" true>>
    Placeholder: Hello! I'm a placeholder. They'll replace me with someone better soon.
    -> How long have you been here?
        Placeholder: Since the second sprint. They keep meaning to.
    -> Who will you be?
        Placeholder: The ticket says: a wise old someone, to be decided. I've been practising the wise part.
        Placeholder: Ask me anything.
        -> What is the meaning of all this?
            Placeholder: ...
            Placeholder: To be decided.
        -> Never mind.
            Placeholder: That was very wise of you.
    -> What are the gauges?
        Placeholder: Gravity, weather and layers. Don't touch them. Last time someone touched gravity, the east went up.
    -> ‹go›
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
